    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d732">

                <pb facs="0993" n="981" sameAs="frus:frus1945v05/pg981"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.24/2–2745</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="21" xml:id="d732-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-02-27">February 27, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Soviet Ambassador called on me this afternoon and, in continuation of the
                    talk which I had last week with the Soviet Chargé d’Affaires, brought up the
                    possibility of the inclusion in the Fourth Protocol of a provision for the
                    application of $300,000,000 for industrial equipment prior to July 1, 1945, but
                    the equipment to be made available to Soviet Russia after July 1, 1945.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph</hi> C. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Grew</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d732-f1" n="21" type="source" xml:id="d732-f1-content">
                <p>This conversation was reported to Moscow in telegram 467, March 2, 1945, 4 p.m.,
                    not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
